    "turn_text": "Make sure to subscribe wherever you download your podcast and, of course, to the premium version of our website as well. Our guest today is U.S. Representative Mark Harris, a Republican representing North Carolina's 8th Congressional District and a member of the Subcommittee on the Constitution and Limited Government. The Committee held a hearing this week on legislative reforms to end lawfare by state and local prosecutors, and it was quite a hearing. Sir, thank you so much for joining us on the Federalist Radio Out. Thank you so much, man. It's a pleasure to be with you. It is a pleasure to have you with us. Give us a little overview because I know there were some sparks on this, but I can't think of too many more important things than dealing with the weaponization of our justice system in America, as we've seen over and over again the last four years. Well, there were some sparks, as you can imagine, during the hearing. We actually had the hearing earlier in the week, and then the next day came back for a markup of bills in the process. And so it was a great conversation. I felt like during the midst of the hearing, just to be able to distinguish these issues that we're facing with the law fair that has taken place. I think the American public has seen it. I think they recognized it. I think when they elected a majority of us in the U.S. House and we flipped the Senate and we put Donald",
